}, {
  "id": "doc_illusion_casting",
  "name": "Illusion Casting (Sensory Deception)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The creation of false images, sounds, or sensations to deceive the senses. An illusionist can conjure phantasmal objects or creatures that appear real but have no true substance. Examples include Minor Illusion (a simple static image or single sound), Silent Image (an illusory object or creature up to a 15-foot cube), or Major Image (a larger, more complex illusion with sound, smell, and temperature). These could make, say, a ferocious tiger seem to appear in a throne room, sending everyone into a panic, or conjure the illusion of a collapsed bridge to deter pursuers. Illusions can also mask things: e.g., an illusion of a wall that isn\u2019t really there, concealing a doorway. Importantly, while illusions can frighten or mislead enemies, they don\u2019t directly cause harm (except in rare cases of psychic illusions). They rely on trickery \u2013 if an enemy suspects and interacts with the illusion (like poking the illusory tiger), they might get a saving throw to see through it. In literature, illusions are often used by trickster characters to avoid fights (merely appearing to have an army, or appearing to be somewhere you\u2019re not).",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Manipulation Abilities (Mental & Physical Manipulation)",
    "function": "manipulation",
    "elements": [],
    "synergies": ["Illusions combine with Stealth \u2013 an illusory distraction (like a phantom sound or duplicate image) can lure guards away while you sneak the other direction. It also pairs with Fear effects: an illusion of something a target fears can impose disadvantage or trigger a fear response even without a dedicated fear spell. Illusions and Environment abilities together are potent: for instance, create illusory flames while an ally casts a heat spell \u2013 foes might think the entire area is ablaze and overreact or flee. Additionally, illusions synergize with Scrying/Divination in a mind-game way: if you know an enemy\u2019s memories (through divination), you can craft eerily specific illusions (like a loved one\u2019s voice calling to them) to manipulate them psychologically."],
