}, {
  "id": "doc_charm_and_compulsion",
  "name": "Charm & Compulsion (Mind Influence)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "Enchantments that influence the thoughts or emotional state of targets, without fully controlling them. A Charm Person spell, for example, makes a humanoid regard the caster as a friendly acquaintance for a time (usually until the spell ends or the caster\u2019s allies harm the target). The charmed creature is less inclined to attack or be hostile to the charmer \u2013 effectively you talk an enemy into standing down or even subtly help you. Unlike domination (below), charm doesn\u2019t allow you to issue complex orders against the target\u2019s nature; it\u2019s more of a befriending/confusion effect. Other compulsion spells could include Suggestion (implanting a single convincing suggestion that the target feels compelled to follow) \u2013 e.g., suggesting \u201cWhy don\u2019t you take the day off from guard duty You look tired,\u201d which if failed save, they\u2019ll do. These abilities are quintessentially non-violent; they aim to avoid combat or conflict by manipulating behavior. In a novel context, this is like Jedi mind tricks (\u201cThese aren\u2019t the droids you\u2019re looking for\u2026\u201d).",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Manipulation Abilities (Mental & Physical Manipulation)",
    "function": "manipulation",
    "elements": ["nature", "arcane"],
    "synergies": ["Pairs extremely well with Social skills (Persuasion/Deception) \u2013 magic gets the target in a receptive state, then good roleplaying seals the deal. Also, charm can be combined with Illusions for deeper deception: e.g., charm a guard to trust you, then use an illusion to appear as their captain giving orders; the guard, charmed and fooled, will obey readily. One must be cautious: if the charm wears off or is broken, the target often realizes they were enchanted \u2013 here a Memory Modification ability (covered next) could erase that suspicion, covering your tracks. So, a powerful combo is: Charm someone to get info, then Modify Memory so they forget being charmed and maybe even remember willingly giving the info, leaving no ill will."],
