  "cooldown": 5,
  "isMagic": true,
  "element": "ice",
  "damage": {
    "base": 0,
    "multiplier": 0,
    "allowZeroDamage": true
  },
  "tags": ["non_damaging", "manipulation", "manipulation_abilities"]
}, {
  "id": "doc_emotional_control",
  "name": "Emotional Control (Calm or Arouse Emotions)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "Abilities that suppress or amplify emotions in targets. For instance, a bard\u2019s music might Inspire Courage (buffing allies by filling them with bravery), which is a positive buff, or conversely, Calm Emotions is a cleric spell that can soothe a crowd, suppressing fear or anger. If two factions are on the verge of fighting, a cast of Calm Emotions could diffuse the hostility, essentially a non-violent resolution. On the other hand, an evil enchanter might use an aura of Despair that makes enemies feel hopeless (mechanically imposing penalties or sapping their will to fight). Unlike charm which targets one creature\u2019s attitude toward the caster, emotional control can affect multiple people and is more about a general mood (not necessarily making them like the caster, just feel a certain way). Fear spells, which cause creatures to panic and run, also fall here \u2013 magically inducing the Frightened condition (creature wants to flee) without directly harming them. These abilities are often area-of-effect and can prevent battles (e.g., calming rioters, or scattering a group of foes in terror so you don\u2019t have to fight them).",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Manipulation Abilities (Mental & Physical Manipulation)",
    "function": "manipulation",
    "elements": ["arcane", "air"],
    "synergies": ["Works well with Illusions or Displays that align with the emotion \u2013 e.g., cast a Fear spell while also casting an illusory image of a terrifying dragon; even if some rational part knows the dragon might not be real, the magically amplified fear can override them. Likewise, a Calm Emotions spell could be combined with Diplomacy skill: you magically remove the anger, then logically persuade the parties to come to an agreement. Emotional manipulation also pairs with Charm/Compulsion: you could calm a guard (removing his aggression) then charm him to be friendly, a one-two that makes him an ally, or inflame someone\u2019s jealousy and then Suggest a course of action related to that emotion. Emotion control essentially sets the stage for other social or mental manipulations to work more effectively."],
    "source": "docx_non_combat_abilities_spells"
  },
