}, {
  "id": "doc_shapeshifting",
  "name": "Shapeshifting (Self-Transformation)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The ability to change one\u2019s own form into something else, typically an animal or another person. Druids are famous for Wild Shape \u2013 for example, at moderate levels a druid can assume the shape of a wolf, bird, or bear that they have seen. This is extremely useful non-combat: as a hawk you can scout from above, as a mouse you can creep through cracks into a locked room, as a horse you can carry allies faster, etc. It can also avoid combat entirely (turn into a harmless animal to sneak by monsters, or into a fierce animal to intimidate but not actually fight). Other types include polymorphing self into even other humanoids (to disguise as someone else) or into elemental forms (becoming living water or fire to slip through barriers). Importantly, while shapeshifting can be used in combat (turning into a strong beast to brawl), here we focus on its utility aspects: mobility, infiltration, escape. A classic scenario: need to eavesdrop on a meeting \u2013 shapeshift into a housecat and curl up under the table. Or escaping jail \u2013 become a tiny insect and slip through the bars.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Manipulation Abilities (Mental & Physical Manipulation)",
    "function": "manipulation",
    "elements": ["fire", "water"],
    "synergies": ["Self-shapeshifting synergizes with Communication abilities: if you turn into an animal, having telepathy or the Speak with Animals ability means you can still coordinate with your team while in beast form. It also pairs with Regeneration in some lore \u2013 e.g., werewolves (shapeshifters) often regenerate quickly; a druid\u2019s wounds might heal faster when they shift back to human. Combining shapeshift with buffs can be wild: casting Haste on a druid in cheetah form yields an incredibly fast creature. Additionally, consider shapeshifting with Illusion backup: if you can only turn into a bear but you want to appear as a specific person, you might physically turn into a humanoid of roughly that size and then use a minor illusion glamor to tweak the details \u2013 a bit contrived, but illustrates multi-ability synergy. Usually, though, shapeshifting is powerful on its own, essentially giving you a suite of creature abilities to avoid conflict (flight, aquatic breathing, keen senses, etc.) at will."],
    "source": "docx_non_combat_abilities_spells"
  },
  "manaCost": 12,
  "cooldown": 5,
  "isMagic": true,
  "element": "fire",
  "damage": {
