  "class": "universal",
  "description": "Changing the size of a creature or object, either growing it larger or shrinking it smaller. The Enlarge/Reduce spell is a good example: you can double a creature\u2019s size (and multiply its weight by 8) or halve it. Enlarging someone makes them stronger (their attacks hit harder due to mass) \u2013 often considered a buff \u2013 and reducing an enemy can weaken their blows (and let you pick them up easily!). But beyond combat, size changing has many uses: Shrinking yourself or an ally can allow entry into small passages, make you harder to spot, or lighten you to cross a flimsy bridge. Enlarging an object can help in construction (enlarge a small piece of stone to become a boulder to block a door, etc.), or allow you to reach something high (make yourself 12 feet tall to grab a ledge). It can even be used for spectacle \u2013 imagine enlarging a coin to a giant size as a distraction or as a temporary platform.",
