  "id": "doc_magnetism",
  "name": "Magnetism (Metal Manipulation)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The ability to manipulate metal via magnetic force. This is narrower than general telekinesis but has unique applications \u2013 effectively, one becomes a human magnet. A magnetism user can yank metallic objects away (disarming all foes armed with steel weapons in a radius), hurl metal objects through the air, or create magnetic shields that deflect metal projectiles (bullets, arrows with iron heads, etc.). They could also assemble or dismantle machines by moving metal parts into place or apart. In modern or steampunk settings, magnetism is incredibly powerful (controlling guns, vehicles, etc.). In a medieval setting, there\u2019s still plenty of metal to influence \u2013 armor (imagine immobilizing a knight by magnet-locking them to the ground), gates, keys, etc. This tends to be non-lethal because it\u2019s about moving things \u2013 you could hurl a bunch of coins at someone to hurt them, but more often you\u2019d rip their armor off or pin them to a wall by their own mail. Offensively, magnetism might cause chaos by flinging debris, but again, it could be used to end fights by de-arming foes.",
