  "id": "doc_fire_manipulation",
  "name": "Fire Manipulation",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The ability to create, shape, and extinguish fire at will. A pyrokinetic or fire mage can summon flames from thin air or ignite flammable objects with a snap of their fingers. They might also control existing fire \u2013 enlarging a campfire into a roaring blaze or snuffing out a torch from across a room. Outside of combat uses include lighting torches or campfires instantly, performing controlled burns (for agriculture or clearing brush), providing warmth in cold environments, or burning debris blocking a path. Fire manipulation can also destroy evidence or hazards (burning away a patch of poisonous mold). While it can be offensive (flames hurt), here we consider its utility: e.g., cauterizing a wound in an emergency, or forging metal tools by heating a forge with magic.",
