  "id": "doc_water_manipulation",
  "name": "Water Manipulation",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "Control over water and liquids \u2013 moving water, changing its shape, or even its state (to some extent, like freezing or vaporizing small amounts). A hydromancer can do things like: draw water from a well without a bucket (make it rise to you), split and part water (like creating a temporary dry path in a stream to cross it), or condense moisture from the air into a usable supply. Non-combat uses are extensive: dousing fires, purifying water (by separating sediment), irrigating crops by channeling river water, or creating sculptures and tools from ice. Underwater breathing could be achieved indirectly (wrap a bubble of air around someone\u2019s head using water/air control). Travel can be aided by water shaping too \u2013 for instance, propelling a boat by forming a current.",
