    "synergies": ["Water is the classic combo element. Water + Lightning yields an electrified water effect \u2013 e.g., in Divinity: Original Sin, \u201cwater + lightning = electrified water, which stuns anyone in it\u201d. So a water manipulator can spread a conductive layer and an ally\u2019s lightning can then incapacitate multiple foes \u2013 a tactical synergy. Water + Cold (with either innate freezing ability or an ally with ice magic) can create ice \u2013 you might flood an area then freeze it to seal a door or form an ice bridge. Water + Earth makes mud, as noted \u2013 a water mage could soften the ground under an enemy\u2019s feet into mud, and if an earth mage then hardens it, the foe\u2019s legs might be stuck. For non-combat synergy: Water + Plant manipulation \u2013 nurturing plants via irrigation, or conversely, water can wash away harmful salt from soil while a plant mage encourages growth. Additionally, Water + Gravity could purify or separate liquids (heavy impurities sink faster in increased gravity water). With Fire, it\u2019s usually oppositional (steam as a side effect or extinguishing each other), but a clever combination can produce steam power or even a thick fog (heat water into fog for concealment). Essentially, water\u2019s versatility allows it to collaborate with nearly any other element for creative problem-solving."],
