  "id": "doc_earth_manipulation",
  "name": "Earth Manipulation",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The power to move and reshape earth and stone. An earthbender can cause the ground to tremble, raise walls or pillars of stone, create pitfalls or close them, and even alter the consistency of earth (hardening soft ground or softening hard ground). In practical terms, this means you can dig tunnels or trenches in minutes, erect earthen barriers for protection, or seal open chasms. Need a shelter Pull up a quick stone hut from the bedrock. Need to reach something high Lift a column of rock to stand on. Earth manipulation is also great for finding or extracting minerals \u2013 sensing ore deposits or unearthing gemstones carefully.",
