    "synergies": ["Earth + Water = mud as mentioned: one might trap enemies or stuck objects in mud, then solidify it. Or use water to wash away loose soil after earth magic cracks the ground. Earth + Plant: an earth mage can till or loosen soil and a plant mage instantly grows crops \u2013 terraforming synergy for agricultural miracles. Earth + Metal (Magnetism): if you can move earth, perhaps you separate metal ores; combined with magnetism, you can refine metals in-ground (earth lifts ore to surface, magnet picks it out). Earth + Gravity: intensifying gravity on earth could cause a localized sinkhole (maybe too combative), or decreasing gravity could let you create larger stone structures without collapse. Earth + Fire: forging is basically this synergy \u2013 use earth to gather and shape raw ore, fire to smelt and refine it. Or in terrain control: use earth to trap someone in a stone encasement, then gently bake it with fire to harden \u2013 now you have a non-lethal prison. With sound (vibrations), an earth mage could detect things via seismic sensing \u2013 perhaps feeling footsteps through the ground from far away. Finally, Earth + Air can produce sandstorms or dust clouds for cover (grind earth to sand, then wind carries it). Earth is solid and foundational, often the starting point for combined effects that require material presence (like giving other elements something to work with). Non-combat highlight: building and engineering tasks become trivial \u2013 one can be a one-person construction crew or miner with earth control."],
