  "id": "doc_weather_control",
  "name": "Weather Control",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A grand ability to influence the weather patterns over an area. This includes summoning rain, storms, fog, wind, or calming such weather. A druid or powerful sorcerer might cast Control Weather, which over ~10 minutes can change weather conditions (within natural limits for the region/season) \u2013 e.g., calling a thunderstorm on a summer day or a blizzard in winter. They can\u2019t pinpoint things like exactly where lightning will strike, but they control the general trend (wind direction, precipitation, temperature). Non-combat uses: end a drought by bringing rain (or create a downpour to douse a widespread fire), ensure safe passage for a ship by invoking a favorable wind and clear skies, or conversely, cover a retreat with heavy fog or a sudden snowstorm. Weather control can prevent natural disasters (calm a hurricane) or unfortunately cause them (though causing would often be combative or at least hostile to someone). It\u2019s a wide-area, strategic ability rather than tactical.",
