  "id": "doc_plant_control",
  "name": "Plant Control (Nature\u2019s Grasp)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The ability to stimulate and direct plant growth or communicate with plant life. A druid or ranger with this power might cause vines and roots to entangle foes or obstacles \u2013 for instance, the Entangle spell causes weeds and vines to sprout from the ground and restrain creatures in an area. In a utility sense, this can be used to bind a wild animal harmlessly or create a barrier of thorny bushes to keep intruders out (without harming them, just making a literal thorn fence). Plant control also means you can encourage crops to grow faster or healthier, restore barren land to fertility, or get trees to move or part \u2013 imagine commanding a dense forest to open a pathway for your group (and then closing behind to thwart followers). Some plant masters can cause flowers to bloom instantly (handy for camouflaging an area or just beautification) or even animate a tree to walk (though that blurs into combat if used aggressively). They could also commune with plants \u2013 e.g., ask a tree if anyone passed by (like how trampled it felt), essentially Speak with Plants.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
