    "function": "elemental",
    "elements": ["water", "nature", "arcane"],
    "synergies": ["Plant + Earth + Water is the trifecta of terraforming \u2013 combine these to reclaim a desert or stop landslides by rooting the soil, etc. For defense, Plant + Poison: a plant controller could cultivate poisonous ivy or hallucinogenic spores and, with air control, disperse them around as a deterrent (again, not directly stabbing anyone, just making an area impassable). Plant + Healing: many herbal remedies come from plants; a plant mage might literally grow medicinal herbs on the spot to treat wounds (synergizing with Herbalism). Plant control also synergizes with Stealth \u2013 one could have grasses bend to conceal the party, or climb into the canopy with vines lifting you. With Wind, you could spread pollen far to propagate certain flora, or conversely blow away harmful spores. And a neat trick: Plant + Illusion \u2013 you might not think to combine those, but e.g., cover an area with dense illusory foliage which then feels real because the plant mage weaves some actual vines within \u2013 making it harder for someone to disbelieve the illusion. More straightforward: Entangle + Fire synergy is more combat (vine holds them, fire scares or hurts them), but non-combat could be using entangle to hold a structure in place while fixing it, or to gently lower something fragile by growing vines under it like a net. Plant control is generally a gentle art that can solve physical problems (climbing, blocking, repairing via roots stabilizing) in harmony with nature, often avoiding violence \u2013 for example, restraining a dangerous creature without injuring it so it can later be released or relocated safely."],
    "source": "docx_non_combat_abilities_spells"
