}, {
  "id": "doc_light_and_darkness_manipulation",
  "name": "Light & Darkness Manipulation",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The power to create, shape, or eliminate light and shadows. On the light side, a mage could conjure globes of light (Dancing Lights, Daylight spells) to illuminate a dark cavern or to banish magical darkness. They might also concentrate light into a beam (like a flashlight or a focused laser for precision cutting, though high-intensity light can burn). On the darkness side, a caster could summon magical darkness that normal light can\u2019t illuminate \u2013 Darkness spell creates a 15-foot radius of pitch black that even torches can\u2019t penetrate, useful for escaping pursuers or blinding enemy sentries (while you might have special vision or a way to see). Non-combat uses: Light manipulation can be used for signaling (flash a Morse code with magical lights), for art (light shows), or to help growth of plants (extend daylight in a greenhouse). Darkness manipulation could cool down an area by blocking sunlight or preserve privacy by covering an area in shadow (could be suspicious though!). It\u2019s also useful against certain monsters (many undead or nocturnal creatures are weakened by sunlight \u2013 a light mage could simulate daylight to make a vampire uncomfortable without direct confrontation, for instance).",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Environmental & Elemental Manipulation",
    "function": "elemental",
    "elements": ["nature", "dark", "arcane"],
    "synergies": ["Light + Illusion: one can make incredibly realistic illusions by properly lighting them; conversely, illusion magic often can create images but not true light \u2013 combining with a light spell can make an illusion visible or more convincing in darkness. Darkness + Silence synergy: plunge an area in darkness and silence at once, and you have basically a perfect, non-lethal, containment field \u2013 anyone inside is blind and deaf until it ends, which can halt aggression. Light + Fire: light can ignite certain magical substances or trigger light-sensitive mechanisms (like some puzzles where shining a beam of light opens a door). Fire already emits light, but a light mage can amplify it or shape it (like making shadow puppets big and intimidating). Darkness + Fear: casting darkness can psychologically unsettle people; if you also have a fear aura or use Intimidation, doing it from the cover of darkness can be extra effective (people fear what they can\u2019t see). Also, Light + Healing: some healing or protective spells are flavored as \u201crays of light\u201d (e.g., lay on hands might have a glow); a light specialist might boost healing by providing a source of pure light (in some literature, sunlight or certain light is needed to heal particular curses or wounds \u2013 e.g., exposing a vampire bite to sunlight in the first minute stops the infection, just a hypothetical). And Darkness + Stealth is obvious synergy \u2013 your thieves and assassins love you if you can blanket the area in darkness (assuming they have a way to see or are okay operating blind with maybe telepathic coordination). In summary, controlling illumination doesn\u2019t cause damage on its own; it shifts the conditions of the environment in your favor \u2013 whether giving you light where you need it (exploration, negating a foe\u2019s darkness) or giving you darkness where you need it (hiding, nullifying a guard\u2019s torch). These abilities can completely avoid fights \u2013 e.g., cast darkness on the guards, slip by unseen; or create a dazzling flash to stun a creature and escape \u2013 all without a lethal exchange."],
