  "id": "doc_might_of_the_ox",
  "name": "Might of the Ox (Strength Enhancement)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A buff that significantly increases physical strength. Whether through a spell like Bull\u2019s Strength (from the classic Enhance Ability suite) or a potion of giant strength, the affected character becomes far stronger than normal \u2013 able to lift and carry much more and hit much harder. In D&D\u2019s Enhance Ability, Bull\u2019s Strength gives advantage on Strength checks and doubles carrying capacity. In practical terms outside combat, this means a person can move heavy obstacles (boulders, portcullises) solo, bend iron bars, or hold up a collapsing roof long enough for others to escape. It\u2019s essentially granting the strength of a creature like an ox or giant to a normal person. This buff often has dramatic but non-lethal uses, like performing superhuman feats of construction or rescue.",
