    "category": "Buff Abilities (Enhancements & Boons)",
    "function": "buff",
    "elements": ["arcane"],
    "synergies": ["Strength buffs pair well with any scenario involving weight or force. Might + Earth Manipulation: if an earth mage shapes a rough tunnel, a strength-buffed ally could rapidly shovel debris out or position support beams that normally would require a team. Might + Grappling: in a non-lethal combat scenario, a super-strong person can grapple and restrain foes easily without hurting them (just pin them down). Might + Jump: raw strength can increase jump distance (in some systems), but pair it with a bit of Air magic (updrafts) or Acrobatics skill and you effectively get a pseudo-Hulk leaping ability to cross gaps without fighting through whatever\u2019s below. Might + Endurance: often when you buff strength, someone will attempt something taxing like holding a heavy gate open \u2013 combining it with an endurance or healing buff means they can sustain the effort longer. In a narrative sense, a strong buffed character can carry multiple allies (perhaps combining with Haste to evacuate people from danger swiftly, one under each arm!). And when negotiating or intimidating, demonstrating feats of strength (bending a spear) can end a fight before it starts as onlookers lose the will to challenge you \u2013 a bit of an Intimidation synergy. Essentially, super strength turns many physically impossible tasks into trivial ones, circumventing challenges that might otherwise require complex solutions or combat (like breaking down a locked door instead of fighting guards for the key).."],
