}, {
  "id": "doc_endurance",
  "name": "Endurance (Bear\u2019s Endurance)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A buff that boosts constitution, stamina, and vitality, allowing someone to withstand hardship, poison, or fatigue much better. In D&D\u2019s Enhance Ability, Bear\u2019s Endurance grants advantage on Constitution checks and also gives some temporary hit points (making the person tougher to hurt). With this, a character can hold their breath longer, survive in extreme temperatures, resist disease or toxin effects better, and generally keep going without rest longer than normal. Non-combat, this could be used to, say, outrun a pursuer over a long distance (the buffed person won\u2019t tire as quickly), survive a night in a freezing blizzard until rescue, or drink a cup of poison without succumbing (handy for diplomacy in fiction when forced into a \u201cprove you\u2019re not poisoning me by drinking it too\u201d scenario). It also helps with things like rowing a boat for hours, digging someone out of a cave-in while dust chokes the air, or enduring the G-forces of a wild teleport or flight.",
