    "function": "buff",
    "elements": ["nature", "air"],
    "synergies": ["Endurance buffs work great with any prolonged activity. Endurance + Haste \u2013 normally haste has that crash, but an endurance buff might mitigate the exhaustion after the haste ends (depending on DM ruling). Endurance + Grappling \u2013 you can maintain a grapple or hold a door shut against enemies far longer. Endurance + Poison Resistance \u2013 stacking a general endurance buff with a specific anti-toxin or Protection from Poison could allow survival of deadly poisons or environmental hazards (endurance to keep bodily functions normal, plus poison resistance to slow the toxin). Endurance + Necromancy resistance \u2013 e.g., enduring life drain effects or maintaining concentration on a spell despite taking damage (Constitution helps with that in D&D concentration checks). If someone\u2019s doing a long ritual, Bear\u2019s Endurance could keep them from collapsing halfway. Endurance + Defense \u2013 combine with things like Stoneskin or Shield of Faith and you get a very tanky individual: high HP, damage resistance, and high AC \u2013 so if a fight breaks out, they can soak it or, in non-combat terms, they can endure a perilous gauntlet (traps, falling rocks, etc.) to reach a goal when a more fragile person could not. The buff basically makes you the marathon man; in story, it could be how a hero drinks the antidote and then carries their allies across a desert without rest \u2013 it blurs combat and non-combat because it keeps you alive and active through any ordeal."],
