  "id": "doc_bless",
  "name": "Bless (Divine Favor)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A holy (or positive) aura that improves allies\u2019 morale and accuracy. The Bless spell affects multiple allies, giving them a small bonus on attack rolls and saving throws (in D&D, each blessed ally can add +1d4 to every attack roll or save they make for the duration). Though described in combat terms, narratively it\u2019s like granting courage, focus and a bit of luck. Outside of direct combat, this could help with things like overcoming fear effects, breaking enchantments (via improved saves), or succeeding at crucial tasks \u2013 e.g., a blessed ally might be more likely to not slip while climbing a cliff or to endure the pain while disarming a magical trap (since saving throws vs. environmental hazards are improved). It\u2019s essentially a general boost to performance under pressure. In social or other challenges, one might stretch it to mean the person feels confident and optimistic, which could indirectly aid charisma checks (though not by raw rules, but a DM might allow that flavor).",
