  "id": "doc_inspiration",
  "name": "Inspiration (Bardic or Leadership Inspiration)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "The act of bolstering an ally\u2019s resolve, skill, or fighting spirit through words, music, or example. A Bard\u2019s Inspiration typically lets them give a creature a special die (e.g., a d6) that the creature can roll later to add to any ability check, attack, or save. Outside of bards, a commander-type character might have a \u201crallying cry\u201d that grants temporary HP or morale bonuses to allies. The key aspect: this is a targeted buff that represents confidence or clarity imparted to the ally. In non-combat scenarios, this could be used to help someone over a mental hurdle (like \u201cYou can do this!\u201d \u2013 granting inspiration to an ally trying to pick a lock or recall lore under pressure). In tense social scenarios, a subtle bardic tune might give the party face the extra boost to not falter in negotiations. In combat (though we\u2019re focusing on non-combat uses), it\u2019s like giving someone the courage to land a decisive blow.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Buff Abilities (Enhancements & Boons)",
    "function": "buff",
    "elements": [],
    "synergies": ["Inspiration + Skill Mastery: if an ally already is good at something (high skill), adding inspiration means they can achieve truly remarkable feats \u2013 say an inspired climber might scale a sheer wall in record time to set up a rope for others. Inspiration + Emotional Control: a leader figure might combine a Calm Emotions to quell panic and then an Inspiration speech to uplift \u2013 net effect: a group of terrified villagers becomes a coordinated bucket brigade to put out a fire instead of scattering. Bardic Inspiration + Cutting Words (a bard\u2019s debuff that imposes penalties on foes) is a bit of a \u201cgood cop, bad cop\u201d vibe \u2013 one ally gets pumped up while the enemy gets roasted and demoralized. As a result, a confrontation might end without violence if the enemy loses the will to fight (because the heroes seem confident and the foe was verbally undermined). Inspiration + Exhaustion mitigation: if someone is on their last legs, a timely inspiration might give them just enough oomph to finish a journey or task before collapsing. Also consider synergy with Divination: if you know via foresight that a certain ally will face a critical challenge soon, you can hold an inspiration for that moment to ensure success (the diviner says \u201ctrust me, you\u2019ll need this boost later\u201d \u2013 meta-gaming in story). Essentially, Inspiration powers from bards or leaders are about the intangible edge \u2013 turning the tide of morale and determination. Many classic tales have moments where a hero\u2019s words rally the troops to avoid a battle (\u201cwe stand down nay, we stand together!\u201d or vice versa to avoid suicide charging \u2013 whichever avoids needless combat). These abilities encapsulate that notion of morale as a weapon/boon."],
