  "name": "Flight (Flying/Levitation Buff)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "Granting the power of flight or levitation to someone who normally can\u2019t. The Fly spell, for example, allows a person to fly at a good speed for several minutes. This is a huge buff in terms of mobility \u2013 it can turn a ground-bound character into an aerial one. Non-combat uses: bypassing obstacles (why fight through guards at a gate when you can fly over the wall at night), reaching high places (rescuing someone from a cliff or tall tree), quickly crossing rivers or dangerous terrain (lava, traps, etc.) without triggering them, and even dramatic entries/exits (flying in to deliver important treaty documents). Levitation, a more limited variant, might only allow up/down movement, but that could still get someone out of a pit or help with repairing a ceiling. Flying an ally also means you can evacuate wounded people or children from a disaster area easily.",
