}, {
  "id": "doc_weakness",
  "name": "Weakness (Enfeeblement)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A curse or effect that saps the physical strength or effectiveness of a target. An example is Ray of Enfeeblement, a spell that causes a creature\u2019s strength-based attacks to do half damage \u2013 essentially their blows land with far less force because their muscles weaken. Another example: a potion of weakness in Skyrim makes an enemy take more damage or deal less damage. Non-combat wise, you could use this to subdue a strong opponent without injuring them \u2013 e.g., enfeeble a raging barbarian so that when they hit, it\u2019s like a child hitting, allowing you to restrain or talk sense into them. It\u2019s also handy for labor situations: prevent a hostile giant from lifting a boulder to throw it by zapping them with weakness so they drop it. If someone is using strength to break something (door, chains), enfeeble them to delay or prevent it. It is a targeted debuff that doesn\u2019t immobilize, but significantly reduces physical threat.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Debuff Abilities (Hindrances & Impairments)",
    "function": "debuff",
    "elements": ["water", "dark", "arcane"],
    "synergies": ["Enfeeblement + Disarm: a weak enemy can\u2019t resist a disarm attempt well \u2013 they have no strength to hold their weapon, making it easier to pluck away (mechanics aside, narratively that fits). Weakness + Grapple: if you enfeeble an opponent, even a smaller person could grapple and hold them because the target\u2019s strength contest is poor \u2013 a means to capture someone alive safely. Weakness + Protection: combining weakening a foe and casting protective buffs on allies ensures that even if the foe tries to fight, they likely can\u2019t hurt anyone \u2013 a great non-lethal outcome where the foe tires out punching your armored, blessed, hearty self and eventually gives up. Weakness + Negotiation: show a brute that their strength means nothing (by magically weakening them mid-brawl) and they might lose the will to fight, making them more amenable to talks. Weakness + Empower (on different targets): a dramatization \u2013 you weaken the enemy\u2019s champion while subtly enhancing the allied champion (maybe via Bless or Giant\u2019s Strength potion) \u2013 when they duel, the enemy\u2019s side is likely to yield seeing their champion easily bested, resolving a larger conflict. Also, Weakness vs. creatures reliant on strength (like a pack animal or a siege ogre) can halt an impending non-human threat \u2013 e.g., an enfeebled dragon might struggle to take off or break through a gate, buying time for a peaceful evacuation or a ritual. Essentially, Weakness-type debuffs are a way to remove the \u201cmight makes right\u201d factor from an equation \u2013 if the bully or monster no longer has overwhelming strength, alternative solutions and dialogues often emerge."],
