  "id": "doc_silence",
  "name": "Silence (Mute Field)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "An ability that eliminates sound in a certain area or on a target. The Silence spell creates a bubble (usually 20-foot radius) where no sound can be made \u2013 people inside can\u2019t speak or shout, and those outside can\u2019t hear anything from inside. This is immensely useful to thwart communication: a cult leader trying to chant a spell \u2013 silenced, no magic comes; guards trying to ring an alarm bell \u2013 no sound; two patrols trying to coordinate \u2013 cut off. It\u2019s also useful to protect others from a dangerous noise (like a banshee\u2019s wail or a thunderous explosion) by casting silence around the source. In diplomacy or trickery, casting silence on yourself or an ally can let you move utterly noiselessly (no clanking armor) or have a private conversation among a group in a crowded room (no one hears you). Offensively, it stops spellcasters from using spells with verbal components, which can avoid a fight by disabling an aggressive mage without hurting them.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Debuff Abilities (Hindrances & Impairments)",
    "function": "debuff",
    "elements": ["lightning", "arcane"],
    "synergies": ["Silence + Darkness was mentioned \u2013 the combo for a quiet, unseen extraction or escape. Silence + Grapple: if you manage to silence an enemy spellcaster and grapple them, they are basically completely unable to pose a threat (many higher-level fights revolve around this combo to non-lethally deal with enemy mages). Silence + Social: if two NPC factions are negotiating and one side starts invoking a ritual or calling for backup, a well-timed silence could prevent escalation (they can\u2019t yell for the ambush to spring, buying you time to talk more). Silence + Bard: ironically, silencing the enemy bard or warhorn can demoralize their side (their buffs and signals fail) while your side\u2019s still function \u2013 psychological edge. Silence + Sleep or Stun: you could knock people out quietly, because normally a body thudding alerts others, but in silence, their collapse is noiseless \u2013 facilitating \u201ctake out the guards one by one without a peep.\u201d Another fun synergy: Silence + Luring \u2013 cast silence on a noisy area (like crunchy leaves or creaky floor) so you can cross it without making a sound then drop silence across the area you left so pursuing enemies can\u2019t call out \u2013 this is like a burglar\u2019s dream tool. Also, Silence on specific individuals: if a particularly loud figure (like an orator inciting a mob or a commander giving orders mid-battle) is silenced, their side loses coordination or morale \u2013 possibly averting a fight or turning it. Overarchingly, Silence is a pacifist\u2019s friend: it prevents dangerous words (no spell incantations, no intimidation shouts, no alarm bells), often stopping violence before it starts or containing it to a limited zone."],
