  "id": "doc_paralysis",
  "name": "Paralysis (Hold Person/Monster)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A strong debuff that freezes the target in place, unable to move or speak. Hold Person paralyzes a humanoid for up to a minute if they fail a save. A paralyzed creature can still see and hear but can\u2019t act (and if you approach them threateningly, their fear might increase). This is akin to an extreme grapple \u2013 you\u2019ve taken them out without harming them. It\u2019s excellent for capturing criminals or stopping a berserker without killing them. They\u2019re conscious and can be reasoned with (though they can\u2019t reply until it wears off), so you could, e.g., hold someone, then tell their allies \u201cWe have your leader at our mercy; let\u2019s talk terms,\u201d potentially ending a conflict. Or hold an assassin mid-stab, then disarm them. It\u2019s a humane way to neutralize dangerous targets.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Debuff Abilities (Hindrances & Impairments)",
    "function": "debuff",
    "elements": [],
    "synergies": ["Paralyze + Disarm is trivial \u2013 a paralyzed person can\u2019t resist you taking their weapon. Paralyze + Monologue: classic villain move is to freeze the heroes and then explain the plan\u2026 but heroes can do the reverse: freeze a foe and then try persuasive conversation (\u201cyou\u2019re not going anywhere, listen to why you should surrender\u2026\u201d). Paralyze + Capture: works with any binding or caging \u2013 you can easily bind someone who\u2019s paralyzed, so when the spell ends they\u2019re already restrained physically (layering non-lethal methods). Hold Monster + Banish: if you can paralyze a rampaging magical beast and then banish it to its home plane, you solve the problem without killing it \u2013 a two-step removal (this is higher magic but a valid synergy to avoid destroying a creature). Paralysis + Cure: if an ally or neutral party is doing something harmful under compulsion (say a werewolf curse or mind control), you could hold them in place so they cause no harm, then work on curing the underlying issue \u2013 synergy with spells that remove curses or diseases. Mass Paralysis (or multiple targets) combined with an intimidating demonstration (like surrounding them with drawn bows) can effectively end a battle: the enemy literally can\u2019t move or fight and sees they are outmaneuvered, so surrender becomes likely once they can speak. Paralysis vs. Spellcasting is great too \u2013 like silence, it prevents verbal and somatic components, so a held mage can\u2019t cast \u2013 but one nice synergy is Paralyze + Memory wipe: hold a spy, modify their memory while they\u2019re held and helpless, then let them go thinking they completed their mission \u2013 conflict solved covertly. Essentially, paralysis is a very direct and decisive debuff that removes an aggressor\u2019s capability completely for a short time, letting the protagonists choose a non-lethal follow-up (like tying up or negotiating)."],
