}, {
  "id": "doc_petrification",
  "name": "Petrification (Turn to Stone)",
  "type": "active",
  "class": "universal",
  "description": "A more severe debuff that turns the target into stone (or another inanimate substance), effectively removing them from action entirely. While usually petrification is seen as a monster ability (like a Medusa\u2019s gaze) or a curse (via high-level magic), a creative hero might have access to a temporary petrify (there are spells like Flesh to Stone). Non-lethally, this is an ultimate hold: the victim is in suspended animation, stone form \u2013 they won\u2019t age or feel anything. This could be used to stop someone who cannot be reasoned with without killing them. For instance, an evil sorcerer about to unleash a world-ending spell \u2013 turn them to stone mid-cast; now you can safely store that statue in a vault indefinitely (hopefully no one breaks it). Or if a giant monster is rampaging, petrify it \u2013 instant statue (perhaps later to be de-petrified and relocated to a safer plane). The downside is, if not reversed, petrification is effectively permanent imprisonment, so ethically it\u2019s heavy \u2013 but in lieu of execution, it\u2019s an alternative punishment.",
  "level": 1,
  "template": {
    "category": "Debuff Abilities (Hindrances & Impairments)",
    "function": "debuff",
    "elements": ["dark", "arcane", "earth"],
    "synergies": ["Petrify + Sculpting: one could literally reshape a petrified foe\u2019s form to something less dangerous, like cut their stone weapons off or move them into a better pose for confinement, before reversing it\u2026 although typically reversing expects the body intact. But maybe an earth bender could partially merge the statue with the ground so when reanimated they\u2019re stuck waist-deep. Petrify + Transport: a stone person can be safely transported (they\u2019re an object now). So you could petrify a friend to carry them through a dangerous area (they won\u2019t suffer thirst or pain as stone), then restore them \u2013 a weird synergy to protect someone through harsh conditions. Petrify + Display: deterrence factor \u2013 \u201cthis was the last guy who attacked our town\u201d (points to stone statue of attacker) \u2013 can ward off others, avoiding future fights. Cure Petrification synergy: if someone good was petrified by a monster, having the cure ready fosters goodwill and avoids conflict with those who might have done something desperate to cure them (like antagonizing a witch for a potion, etc.). In terms of multi-debuff combos, petrification is usually standalone \u2013 you don\u2019t need to paralyze someone then petrify (though that ensures they don\u2019t dodge the gaze, if that\u2019s how it\u2019s delivered). Perhaps Sleep then Petrify \u2013 if you want to secretly petrify someone, put them asleep so they won\u2019t know who did it when/if they\u2019re restored. Honestly, petrification is the ultimate neutralization short of killing: synergy with anything mainly in how you handle the statue afterward \u2013 e.g., Stone to Flesh (undo) combined with immediate binding to capture the person alive after transport. It\u2019s risky but a potent non-lethal tactic if used with the right intentions and follow-up."],
