    "elements": ["arcane", "earth"],
    "synergies": ["Stoneskin + Weakness Debuff on enemies \u2013 combine reduced enemy damage output with your damage resistance and you become nearly invulnerable to their attacks, potentially causing them to give up in despair of scratching you. Stoneskin + Healing: even if some damage gets through, a quick healing refresh plus resistance means you can outlast opponents without striking them \u2013 essentially a strategy to tank until they yield. Stoneskin + Grapple: you can safely grapple opponents under heavy fire because their blows on you during the grapple are minor; you can restrain people without worry about their friends\u2019 swords much. Iron Body + Peaceful approach: one could deliberately let an enemy strike their stony self, show no pain, and say \u201cI do not wish to fight\u201d \u2013 a bit of a Dr. Manhattan move; this psychological play could make intelligent foes reassess (this works best if you could also conjure Elemental Aura or something for show \u2013 but even just stone skin cracks their blades which can freak them out). Damage resistance + Environment: if a building is collapsing or a carriage is wrecking, a stoneskinned individual can shield others with their body, taking minimal harm \u2013 purely rescue-applicable synergy with heroism. And if you have Stoneskin + actual Stone Shape synergy \u2013 a druid might take on a barkskin (similar concept) and also control plants to entangle foes \u2013 they become an implacable, uninjurable warden figure causing entangling roots to stop a fight. Mechanically, stacking different resistances (like via stoneskin and a racial trait or another spell) can reduce damage to 1/4 or 0 \u2013 a powerful combination to ensure no one on your side gets killed by a panicked act of aggression, giving time to settle things calmly."],
